1
00:00:24,916 --> 00:00:27,083
How can we impact that exact location?

2
00:00:29,708 --> 00:00:31,375
Sir, there's some confusion.

3
00:00:32,625 --> 00:00:36,125
We've got today's coordinates back
for tomorrow's op, including Point 4065.

4
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:40,750
Army told us to hold because they wanted
to commence the ground assault--

5
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,083
They did.

6
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,041
But as soon as they climbed the hill,

7
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:45,083
they were ambushed.

8
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:48,666
Unfortunately, not just 4065,

9
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:51,000
that's the story of
every single peak we've bombed.

10
00:00:51,583 --> 00:00:52,833
How is it possible, sir?

11
00:00:52,916 --> 00:00:55,166
Seventy percent of our bombs
have been on target.

12
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,875
Bombs are striking the peaks,

13
00:00:56,958 --> 00:00:59,166
but with
a 100-to-150-metre margin of error,

14
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:02,000
they're not directly destroying
the enemy sangars.

15
00:01:02,083 --> 00:01:04,583
And we've also learned
from the enemy's RT intercepts

16
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:08,375
that the shrapnel from our bomb blasts
are unable to penetrate the sangar rocks.

17
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:11,250
So their strategy
has become very simple now.

18
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:13,416
The moment they hear our jets approaching,

19
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:15,250
they take cover inside their sangars.

20
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:17,958
And when our Army climbs,
they come right back out.

21
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:21,708
That means

22
00:01:22,625 --> 00:01:25,833
our sophisticated high-altitude strategy

23
00:01:27,208 --> 00:01:29,833
is being neutralized by prehistoric rocks.

24
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,541
In the Kargil sector, the Pakistan Army

25
00:01:33,625 --> 00:01:36,875
has committed gross atrocities
against our fallen soldiers.

26
00:01:36,958 --> 00:01:40,041
According to defense sources,
the bodies do not just bear bullet wounds,

27
00:01:40,125 --> 00:01:42,833
the savagery includes
burning of flesh with cigarettes,

28
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:47,250
rupturing eardrums with hot rods,
gouging out eyes, and mutilating limbs.

29
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:49,958
Amid growing public outrage,
the Indian Army has promised

30
00:01:50,041 --> 00:01:55,666
a befitting reply to the Pakistan Army's
inhuman message within 48 hours.

31
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,666
Within 48 hours?

32
00:01:58,708 --> 00:02:01,041
Even 48 years wouldn't be enough.

33
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:13,500
I'm sorry.

34
00:03:16,083 --> 00:03:17,000
We tried.

35
00:03:26,708 --> 00:03:27,708
Jai Hind, sir.

36
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:31,458
One of the captive Pakistani soldiers
has regained consciousness, sir.

37
00:03:32,416 --> 00:03:33,250
Tony, I'll see you.

38
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,583
Let us through.

39
00:03:38,666 --> 00:03:40,625
We won't spare them.

40
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:45,208
Boys!

41
00:03:45,833 --> 00:03:47,125
Let us go, sir!

42
00:03:47,208 --> 00:03:50,208
They deserve the same treatment
that they gave to our brothers.

43
00:03:50,291 --> 00:03:51,416
This is the Indian Army!

44
00:03:53,416 --> 00:03:55,083
We're all seething with rage.

45
00:03:56,250 --> 00:03:59,208
But whatever we'll do,
will be on the battlefield.

46
00:04:00,041 --> 00:04:01,833
Not with a half-dead enemy like this.

47
00:04:11,625 --> 00:04:14,458
You have two options. Either you confess,

48
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:16,500
or my men outside are waiting for you.

49
00:04:17,583 --> 00:04:19,583
They all know you're from 12 NLI.

50
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:23,916
If I give them a free hand--

51
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,291
Go ahead, sir.

52
00:04:27,041 --> 00:04:28,833
I have killed their brothers.

53
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:31,875
Aren't you afraid of dying?

54
00:04:31,958 --> 00:04:34,041
How many times
will you kill a dead person?

55
00:04:34,125 --> 00:04:36,375
So what did a dead person get
by doing all this?

56
00:04:37,833 --> 00:04:38,833
The same thing

57
00:04:40,166 --> 00:04:41,416
that you get.

58
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:44,541
A salary.

59
00:04:47,583 --> 00:04:49,125
Now you won't even get that.

60
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:54,458
The Commander of the 12 NLI,
the DGMO, General Musharraf,

61
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:56,583
they've all publicly stated

62
00:04:57,208 --> 00:04:59,708
that you're not part
of the Pakistani Army.

63
00:04:59,791 --> 00:05:01,833
Which country's army
were you fighting for?

64
00:05:01,916 --> 00:05:04,458
One that is refusing to even acknowledge
your existence?

65
00:05:04,541 --> 00:05:06,250
You'll rot in a prison here.

66
00:05:06,875 --> 00:05:10,916
Your family won't even get to know
where you vanished,

67
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:13,833
or how you passed away.

68
00:05:22,083 --> 00:05:23,083
Sir,

69
00:05:24,625 --> 00:05:26,833
I want to make a statement.

70
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:36,166
So after this confession, do you think

71
00:05:36,958 --> 00:05:38,708
we'll get permission to cross the LoC?

72
00:05:38,791 --> 00:05:41,666
Yes, we've seized all their Army IDs.

73
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:43,625
And military documents. In fact,

74
00:05:44,291 --> 00:05:48,416
we've even seized the Stinger missiles
they used to attack you.

75
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:54,083
But if a country's army
is blatantly disowning its own soldiers,

76
00:05:55,083 --> 00:05:57,083
what's the use of that evidence?

77
00:05:59,833 --> 00:06:00,791
I'm surprised.

78
00:06:00,875 --> 00:06:03,291
-I don't think that I've ever--
-Sartaj.

79
00:06:04,666 --> 00:06:07,750
Can I take a look at those SAMs?

80
00:06:21,708 --> 00:06:24,208
There's no radar cueing in this.

81
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:29,666
Sir.

82
00:06:33,458 --> 00:06:34,375
Sartaj.

83
00:06:37,541 --> 00:06:40,333
The Army might not
have to cross the LoC now.

84
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:44,125
Because we won't have to fly
above the clouds.

85
00:06:44,708 --> 00:06:47,208
Now we can hit them from below.

86
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:50,708
Won't that put you
in the range of their SAMs?

87
00:06:50,791 --> 00:06:52,166
Isn't that too risky, Tony?

88
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:53,708
They're heat-seeking missiles.

89
00:06:54,333 --> 00:06:56,125
They have no radar cueing.

90
00:06:56,208 --> 00:06:58,000
They have to lock the target visually.

91
00:06:58,083 --> 00:07:01,083
When we won't be visible at night,
how will they lock on to us?

92
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:04,833
Sartaj, I need a secure line.

93
00:07:05,416 --> 00:07:08,666
Chou, you're flying tonight, right?

94
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:10,458
-Yes, sir.
-One change.

95
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,583
I will fly with you.

96
00:07:13,666 --> 00:07:15,833
We have to do a small experiment.

97
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,625
Releasing in three, two, one…

98
00:07:28,708 --> 00:07:30,250
Now! Bombs away.

99
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,125
Bombs away.

100
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,416
Job done, Arrows. Return to base now.

101
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,333
Copy that.

102
00:07:58,666 --> 00:08:00,791
Arrow 1, confirm losing altitude.

103
00:08:00,875 --> 00:08:02,791
-Check intention.
-Negative, sir.

104
00:08:02,875 --> 00:08:04,583
We're still above the clouds.

105
00:08:04,666 --> 00:08:06,500
Maybe some glitch in the radar, sir.

106
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:16,333
Get into the sangars! Quick!

107
00:08:16,416 --> 00:08:17,458
Move! Move! Move!

108
00:08:24,166 --> 00:08:26,416
-Sir, communication's secure on channel 2.
-Copy that.

109
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,875
-Let's enter the target valley.
-Roger that.

110
00:08:33,875 --> 00:08:35,458
1500 meters above the target.

111
00:08:35,541 --> 00:08:37,166
The peak is visible, but not the sangar.

112
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,958
-Let's go further down, Chou.
-Roger, sir.

113
00:08:40,041 --> 00:08:42,625
Doesn't that sound
a little closer than usual today?

114
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:44,708
Chou, do you see anything?

115
00:08:45,708 --> 00:08:47,750
Negative. Let's go further down.

116
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,541
Okay, Chou. But let's be careful.

117
00:08:49,625 --> 00:08:52,083
-We're in their missile range now.
-Roger that.

118
00:08:59,833 --> 00:09:01,208
Okay, that's it, Chou.

119
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:03,791
Target acquired, 1,000 meters.
Let's get the hell out of here.

120
00:09:03,875 --> 00:09:05,125
Roger that, sir.

121
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,916
Sir, I've checked the model
of their missiles.

122
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,500
They don't have radar homing.

123
00:09:12,583 --> 00:09:14,166
They are heat-seeking missiles.

124
00:09:14,250 --> 00:09:16,625
Which means we can use that
to our advantage.

125
00:09:16,708 --> 00:09:19,750
By flying below the clouds at night,
we can hit their sangars directly.

126
00:09:19,833 --> 00:09:21,333
Sorry, come again, Tony.

127
00:09:21,416 --> 00:09:24,916
You want to do visually guided bombing
at night in these mountains?

128
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,458
We're in moon phase, sir.

129
00:09:26,541 --> 00:09:28,875
The white peaks shine at night.

130
00:09:28,958 --> 00:09:30,791
Visibility isn't a problem.

131
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:33,375
But, Tony,
by the time you finish the trials,

132
00:09:33,458 --> 00:09:35,083
the moon cycle would have ended.

133
00:09:35,166 --> 00:09:38,375
We'll have to wait another 15 days,
and we don't have that much time.

134
00:09:38,458 --> 00:09:40,041
I'm sorry.

135
00:09:40,125 --> 00:09:41,583
But in tonight's bombing run,

136
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,666
we've already conducted the trial.

137
00:09:45,791 --> 00:09:47,125
We can start right away.

138
00:09:47,208 --> 00:09:49,166
That was reckless, Tony.

139
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,416
But they will never expect this.

140
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:53,083
So, let's do it.

141
00:09:54,458 --> 00:09:57,500
Low-altitude night bombing
is officially on.

142
00:10:19,541 --> 00:10:21,500
We're in the sector now. Let's go down.

143
00:10:21,583 --> 00:10:22,708
Roger.

144
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,000
Descending now.

145
00:10:35,875 --> 00:10:37,833
They're coming in close again.

146
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,916
Captain. Get the SAM.

147
00:10:43,416 --> 00:10:44,250
Something is fishy.

148
00:10:45,458 --> 00:10:47,416
We know nothing about their plan.

149
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:50,083
We should hide in the sangars.

150
00:10:51,125 --> 00:10:53,708
If they're daring to enter
our missile range again,

151
00:10:55,083 --> 00:10:55,958
then like last time,

152
00:10:56,875 --> 00:10:58,291
we will bring them down again.

153
00:10:58,375 --> 00:10:59,458
Get the other SAM too.

154
00:10:59,541 --> 00:11:02,375
And, everyone else,
hide in the sangars! Quickly!

155
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:22,000
Two thousand meters above the target.

156
00:11:22,083 --> 00:11:24,833
-Let's go down to 1,000.
-Roger.

157
00:11:33,458 --> 00:11:34,583
Hurry up!

158
00:11:36,541 --> 00:11:39,875
-Stay sharp, they can come from anywhere.
-Sir, where do we aim?

159
00:11:43,083 --> 00:11:45,125
Arrow 2, I have a visual of the peak.

160
00:11:45,208 --> 00:11:46,375
Visual confirmed, Arrow 1.

161
00:11:46,458 --> 00:11:50,375
-Sir, they're coming from this direction.
-Take aim.

162
00:11:55,416 --> 00:11:57,625
Arrow 2, stand by to acquire target.

163
00:11:57,708 --> 00:11:58,625
On stand by.

164
00:11:58,708 --> 00:12:00,541
-Can you see the jets?
-No, sir.

165
00:12:00,625 --> 00:12:01,625
It's too dark.

166
00:12:07,625 --> 00:12:09,375
They're coming straight at us, sir.

167
00:12:11,666 --> 00:12:12,625
Try to get a lock.

168
00:12:12,708 --> 00:12:14,750
Yes, sir, trying to lock on.

169
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:15,958
But I'm not able to.

170
00:12:18,333 --> 00:12:21,916
Arrow 2, after release,
you've six seconds to climb up.

171
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:22,833
Copy that.

172
00:12:22,916 --> 00:12:25,666
If we fire without
locking onto the target, we'll miss it.

173
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:27,416
But we've got no other option.

174
00:12:28,708 --> 00:12:31,000
-Arrow 2, bombs on standby.
-Roger.

175
00:12:32,541 --> 00:12:33,833
Fire!

176
00:12:36,458 --> 00:12:37,291
Bombs away.

177
00:12:37,375 --> 00:12:38,500
Bombs away!

178
00:12:40,541 --> 00:12:43,708
Pull up. Exercise caution. Reheat.

179
00:13:01,916 --> 00:13:04,958
I testify there is no god but Allah…

180
00:13:17,916 --> 00:13:21,875
Flying Officer Dhali, you've became
the youngest pilot in the Indian Air Force

181
00:13:21,958 --> 00:13:24,291
to carry out a low-altitude
night bombing mission.

182
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:27,666
Thank you for trusting me, sir.
This was a real honor.

183
00:13:37,333 --> 00:13:39,083
Boys, you've done it.

184
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:44,583
Your bombs have annihilated
the enemy positions at Point 4065.

185
00:13:45,083 --> 00:13:47,708
The Army will reclaim that peak
within 24 hours.

186
00:13:48,375 --> 00:13:51,041
This will change
the face of the Kargil war.

187
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:57,041
It was just one peak tonight.

188
00:14:00,291 --> 00:14:02,375
There are still
ten moonlit nights left, sir.

189
00:14:06,416 --> 00:14:07,541
Bombs away!

190
00:14:08,750 --> 00:14:10,083
Bombs away!

191
00:14:17,666 --> 00:14:20,625
Sir, we've lost Bashir post too.
That means we can no longer send supplies

192
00:14:20,708 --> 00:14:22,958
to any of our positions
in the Yaldor Sector.

193
00:14:23,041 --> 00:14:26,000
The Kargil War has been underway
for nearly two months now.

194
00:14:26,083 --> 00:14:30,333
And with the Indian Air Force's
low-altitude night bombing campaign,

195
00:14:30,416 --> 00:14:33,541
the tide of the war appears
to be turning in India's favor.

196
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:36,458
Amid continuous bombardment
by the Indian Air Force,

197
00:14:36,541 --> 00:14:39,333
the mountains of Kargil now echo
with the thunder of Bofors guns.

198
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:41,958
Armed with Bofors artillery,
the Indian Army

199
00:14:42,041 --> 00:14:44,916
is shelling enemy positions
around the clock.

200
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:49,625
The defenses of the enemy
have crumbled owing to relentless pressure

201
00:14:49,708 --> 00:14:51,500
maintained by our ground forces.

202
00:14:51,583 --> 00:14:53,958
and the heavy attrition
caused on the enemy

203
00:14:54,041 --> 00:14:55,625
by the effective air strikes

204
00:14:55,708 --> 00:14:58,916
and the pounding
undertaken by our artillery.

205
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,166
While Pakistan continues to suffer
heavy losses on the battlefield,

206
00:15:02,250 --> 00:15:04,666
its diplomatic position
is deteriorating as well.

207
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:07,958
Pakistan's claim that the fighters
in Kargil are Mujahideen

208
00:15:08,041 --> 00:15:09,666
has completely fallen apart.

209
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:11,958
Statements from captured soldiers
have made it clear

210
00:15:12,041 --> 00:15:13,291
that these are not Mujahideen,

211
00:15:13,375 --> 00:15:15,333
but regular soldiers
of the Pakistani Army.

212
00:15:15,416 --> 00:15:18,000
I'm a soldier
of the 12th Northern Light Infantry.

213
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,791
In the beginning, we had plenty of food

214
00:15:20,875 --> 00:15:22,458
and ammunition,

215
00:15:22,541 --> 00:15:25,500
but when the Indian Army
launched its attack,

216
00:15:25,583 --> 00:15:27,625
our superiors abandoned us.

217
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:33,625
If the Indian Army hadn't captured us,
we would've starved to death, sir.

218
00:15:33,708 --> 00:15:35,208
General Zia.

219
00:15:36,875 --> 00:15:39,625
Remove his name from all military records.

220
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:42,791
And tell Hassan
that any troops sent forward

221
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:46,500
must have their military IDs confiscated.

222
00:15:47,541 --> 00:15:49,583
Are we even winning this war?

223
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:56,000
Sir, when have they ever told us the truth
about this operation?

224
00:15:56,583 --> 00:16:00,833
If you want to see the truth of this war,
you'll have to come with me, Mian sahib.

225
00:16:01,375 --> 00:16:05,458
Following two weeks
of relentless joint operations

226
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:08,500
by the Army and Air Force,
India has recaptured

227
00:16:08,583 --> 00:16:11,125
almost all the Pakistan army
occupied peaks in Kargil.

228
00:16:11,208 --> 00:16:13,375
However, some crucial peaks
in Drass and Batalik,

229
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:17,916
such as Tiger Hill and Point 4875,
still remain under Pakistani control.

230
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:39,291
Welcome to Skardu, sir.

231
00:16:40,208 --> 00:16:44,625
Mian sahib has come to see the reality of
this war with his own eyes, Gen. Hassan.

232
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:47,541
It would be better not to hide anything.

233
00:16:49,291 --> 00:16:50,375
Right, sir.

234
00:16:50,875 --> 00:16:52,708
Let's head to the officers' mess.

235
00:16:53,333 --> 00:16:54,875
I'll give you the complete update.

236
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,500
General Hassan, the truth of democracy
is revealed at the polling booth

237
00:17:01,125 --> 00:17:04,833
and the reality of war in the hospital.

238
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:20,333
Sir, this tent was empty till yesterday.

239
00:17:20,416 --> 00:17:23,250
But today, the Indian Air Force
launched a major attack,

240
00:17:24,083 --> 00:17:26,625
inflicting heavy casualties on our troops.

241
00:17:26,708 --> 00:17:29,166
Otherwise, everything
is under control, sir.

242
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:30,416
Pakistan is winning the war.

243
00:17:52,083 --> 00:17:53,583
Is this how we're winning the war?

244
00:17:56,791 --> 00:17:58,416
Shame on an army like this,

245
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:01,083
that cannot stand by its own soldiers.

246
00:18:11,791 --> 00:18:15,000
Who allowed Mian sahib into the base?

247
00:18:15,083 --> 00:18:19,458
When he isn't giving any support
from Islamabad, then he has no right--

248
00:18:19,541 --> 00:18:22,333
Sir, we have lost Aqeel post.

249
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:26,416
-Indian Air Force is now attacking at--
-Aziz has briefed me on everything.

250
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:29,000
Don't miss the big picture, Hassan.

251
00:18:29,083 --> 00:18:31,625
Sir, the big picture is this,
that we had no idea

252
00:18:31,708 --> 00:18:34,708
that such a small operation
would spiral into such a large-scale war.

253
00:18:35,375 --> 00:18:36,708
Every assessment we made

254
00:18:36,791 --> 00:18:39,750
about the Indian Army
and the Indian Air Force has proven wrong.

255
00:18:39,833 --> 00:18:42,208
And now the Indian Army and Air Force

256
00:18:42,291 --> 00:18:43,875
are ready to fight to the death.

257
00:18:43,958 --> 00:18:46,833
I want solutions, not complaints.

258
00:18:47,583 --> 00:18:49,083
There's only one solution, sir.

259
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,750
I think we should withdraw from this war.

260
00:18:55,041 --> 00:18:59,666
Hassan, it was your idea
to capture all those Indian posts, right?

261
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:02,791
And I take full responsibility
for the loss of this war, sir.

262
00:19:04,166 --> 00:19:05,166
I am sorry, sir.

263
00:19:06,416 --> 00:19:10,166
Now, I'll not send
any of my soldiers forward.

264
00:19:10,916 --> 00:19:13,541
My conscience
doesn't allow me to do this, sir.

265
00:19:16,666 --> 00:19:17,750
General Hassan,

266
00:19:19,333 --> 00:19:24,208
I hereby relieve you and your conscience
from this operation.

267
00:19:24,708 --> 00:19:28,291
Hand over all your responsibilities
to General Mahmud.

268
00:19:31,125 --> 00:19:32,208
That will be all.

269
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:34,083
Sir.

270
00:19:41,958 --> 00:19:44,333
Pervez, is everything okay?

271
00:19:47,291 --> 00:19:48,291
Everything is fine.

272
00:19:50,583 --> 00:19:53,958
Pervez, Pakistan Air Force
will not cross the LoC.

273
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:58,416
So this means

274
00:19:59,041 --> 00:20:00,750
the Pakistan Air Force

275
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:04,000
will do nothing
in this country's biggest operation.

276
00:20:04,083 --> 00:20:06,833
Did you consult the Air Force and Navy

277
00:20:06,916 --> 00:20:08,833
before starting all of this?

278
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:10,541
Forget consultation.

279
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:13,125
You didn't even think
it necessary to inform us.

280
00:20:13,208 --> 00:20:15,791
And now, when your plan is failing,

281
00:20:15,875 --> 00:20:18,791
you suddenly remember
the Pakistan Air Force.

282
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:24,083
Then we have to hand it
to the Indian Air Force, Mehdi sahib.

283
00:20:25,125 --> 00:20:26,416
Mehdi sahib,

284
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:28,083
the Indian Air Force

285
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:31,666
must have also
joined this operation overnight, right?

286
00:20:32,541 --> 00:20:35,041
As Air Chief, my answer is clear.

287
00:20:35,125 --> 00:20:37,500
In such terrain, I will not send my pilots

288
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,125
on suicide missions.

289
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:44,375
But, Pervez, as your friend,
I can do something

290
00:20:44,458 --> 00:20:47,916
that will prevent the Indian Air Force
from targeting your sangars.

291
00:20:59,083 --> 00:21:00,833
Arrow 2, preparing to descend.

292
00:21:00,916 --> 00:21:01,875
Roger.

293
00:21:09,666 --> 00:21:12,375
-Arrow 2, approaching target.
-On your tail, sir.

294
00:21:25,583 --> 00:21:27,291
There. Aim over there.

295
00:21:34,083 --> 00:21:36,500
-Approaching target. Stay on my tail.
-Roger.

296
00:21:37,291 --> 00:21:38,333
They're here.

297
00:21:41,041 --> 00:21:43,708
Arrow 2, bombs on standby.

298
00:21:57,625 --> 00:21:59,125
Missile! Pull up! Pull up! Pull up!

299
00:21:59,208 --> 00:22:01,166
The missile's effective range
is 10,000 feet.

300
00:22:01,250 --> 00:22:02,666
If we climb, it'll fall behind.

301
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:04,291
Copy that.

302
00:22:06,416 --> 00:22:09,125
-Pull up! Keep pulling up!
-Pulling up!

303
00:22:13,375 --> 00:22:14,541
Hard right!

304
00:22:27,916 --> 00:22:29,333
What the hell?

305
00:22:29,416 --> 00:22:30,958
How are they able to aim in the dark?

306
00:22:31,041 --> 00:22:32,208
I don't know, sir.

307
00:22:32,291 --> 00:22:33,708
Thankfully, you spotted it in time.

308
00:22:33,791 --> 00:22:36,708
We were lucky. The darkness of night
helped me spot it quickly.

309
00:22:36,791 --> 00:22:38,875
Let's get the hell out of here, Arrow 2.

310
00:22:48,875 --> 00:22:49,708
Sir.

311
00:22:51,291 --> 00:22:52,375
Jai Hind, sir.

312
00:22:52,458 --> 00:22:53,375
At ease.

313
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:04,875
Military Intelligence
has intercepted an RT conversation

314
00:23:04,958 --> 00:23:07,791
between Skardu Base and Point 4875.

315
00:23:08,666 --> 00:23:09,708
Please.

316
00:23:13,041 --> 00:23:14,750
Base to 4875, fighters approaching.

317
00:23:14,833 --> 00:23:16,458
Two fighter jets are approaching.

318
00:23:16,541 --> 00:23:17,541
-Get the SAM.
-Okay, sir.

319
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:19,333
Tell me their position and directions.

320
00:23:19,416 --> 00:23:22,583
060 radial, cruising 1,650 kph.

321
00:23:22,666 --> 00:23:25,333
Expect visual contact in 30 seconds.

322
00:23:27,166 --> 00:23:30,375
The Pakistan Air Force
is installing radars near the peaks.

323
00:23:31,291 --> 00:23:34,125
Now, if our jets fly low over Drass,

324
00:23:34,208 --> 00:23:36,333
the enemy will know their exact heading.

325
00:23:36,416 --> 00:23:38,333
This changes everything.

326
00:23:39,541 --> 00:23:41,791
Our surprise element has been compromised.

327
00:23:41,875 --> 00:23:46,875
We wanted to reclaim Point 5280
in the last sorties of the moon cycle.

328
00:23:46,958 --> 00:23:51,625
Because this peak in Kaksar
was their link to Drass and Batalik.

329
00:23:51,708 --> 00:23:55,041
Not only was this choking NH1
for the Indian Army,

330
00:23:55,125 --> 00:23:58,166
but it's also clear
from Military Intelligence now

331
00:23:58,250 --> 00:24:01,666
that this is the route
for Pakistan Army's fresh reinforcements

332
00:24:01,750 --> 00:24:05,916
to all Drass and Batalik peaks,
including Tiger Hill.

333
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,916
We're down to two choices.

334
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:11,416
Either the Mirage 2000 strikes
from outside the missile range,

335
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:15,875
or the Army climbs inch by inch
and fights a long war.

336
00:24:15,958 --> 00:24:17,833
This will really hurt us.

337
00:24:17,916 --> 00:24:21,666
But there are no
unconventional strategies left to try.

338
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:24,875
It's time for the Golden Arrows
to stand down.

339
00:24:25,541 --> 00:24:26,625
Tony.

340
00:24:28,916 --> 00:24:29,916
Yes, sir.

341
00:24:46,208 --> 00:24:47,291
Sir.

342
00:24:48,041 --> 00:24:49,750
We can hit 5280.

343
00:24:52,750 --> 00:24:54,500
What did you not understand, Baldy?

344
00:24:55,541 --> 00:24:58,875
They have radars now.
Patney sir just explained that.

345
00:24:58,958 --> 00:25:01,625
Exactly, sir. We can trick those radars.

346
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:04,583
Arrows, we've done this before.

347
00:25:05,291 --> 00:25:07,083
Ahuja sir's Transport Jet strategy.

348
00:25:07,166 --> 00:25:08,291
Yes.

349
00:25:08,375 --> 00:25:09,875
We can do it, sir.

350
00:25:09,958 --> 00:25:11,541
Sir, and we should do it today.

351
00:25:11,625 --> 00:25:13,375
There's only one moonlit night left, sir.

352
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:15,708
Ahuja sir trained us
for this very day, sir.

353
00:25:17,125 --> 00:25:18,208
Trained you.

354
00:25:19,166 --> 00:25:20,541
Where? When?

355
00:25:21,083 --> 00:25:24,041
In the flatlands?
In daytime? In peacetime?

356
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,500
The Transport Jet formation
is a very difficult formation in itself.

357
00:25:29,125 --> 00:25:32,833
Right now, we have to fly
in the world's most dangerous mountains,

358
00:25:32,916 --> 00:25:34,041
and that too at night.

359
00:25:34,125 --> 00:25:36,750
In the middle of a war. Get real, boys.

360
00:25:38,708 --> 00:25:39,708
Sir…

361
00:25:40,625 --> 00:25:42,791
Whatever we've done in this war so far,

362
00:25:42,875 --> 00:25:45,625
day bombing, night bombing,
high altitude, low altitude,

363
00:25:46,291 --> 00:25:48,000
we hadn't practiced for that either.

364
00:25:48,083 --> 00:25:49,500
That was different, Dhali.

365
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:53,166
In this type of terrain,
such a difficult formation requires

366
00:25:53,250 --> 00:25:55,166
a completely different type of readiness.

367
00:25:55,250 --> 00:25:56,583
And we are, sir.

368
00:25:57,083 --> 00:25:58,125
We are fully ready.

369
00:25:58,208 --> 00:26:01,125
Baldy, you haven't flown
a single sortie here.

370
00:26:02,166 --> 00:26:04,041
I'm sorry, sir, but that's not my fault.

371
00:26:05,375 --> 00:26:07,416
I've memorized every map ten times over.

372
00:26:07,500 --> 00:26:10,083
But you didn't give me
even a single sortie.

373
00:26:10,750 --> 00:26:12,083
Which is fine. That's your call.

374
00:26:12,166 --> 00:26:14,458
But readiness
is not about the number of sorties.

375
00:26:14,541 --> 00:26:15,958
Madhavi is pregnant, Baldy.

376
00:26:27,416 --> 00:26:30,375
Sir. I don't see the connection, sir.

377
00:26:31,291 --> 00:26:32,458
That's my personal matter.

378
00:26:33,041 --> 00:26:35,208
This can't be the reason
to stop me from flying.

379
00:26:40,875 --> 00:26:42,041
Baldy is right.

380
00:26:42,666 --> 00:26:45,458
This is the life
we all signed up for, sir.

381
00:26:46,125 --> 00:26:47,791
Let this be my call, sir.

382
00:26:48,458 --> 00:26:49,500
Baldy should fly.

383
00:26:53,083 --> 00:26:54,791
Sir, training or no training,

384
00:26:54,875 --> 00:26:57,958
one thing we've definitely learned
is how to back each other up.

385
00:26:58,791 --> 00:27:01,625
Sir, you told me once.
No one's ever ready for war.

386
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:05,000
If we'll go down, we'll go together, sir.

387
00:27:20,333 --> 00:27:23,500
Chou, prepare the jets.

388
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,458
The boys are ready.

389
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:32,750
Arrows,

390
00:27:33,750 --> 00:27:35,708
it'll be my honor to lead you.

391
00:27:40,541 --> 00:27:45,000
Boys, we can fool them
with a Transport Jet formation,

392
00:27:45,083 --> 00:27:47,750
but for two to three minutes at most.

393
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:52,291
So right after takeoff,
we'll split into four pairs

394
00:27:52,375 --> 00:27:54,875
and approach through different valleys.

395
00:27:54,958 --> 00:27:57,958
We'll fly low, below the ridgelines,
staying deep in the valleys

396
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:00,916
so their radars can't detect us.

397
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,041
We must stay perfectly in sync
through the valleys,

398
00:28:04,625 --> 00:28:08,875
so we all reach Delta Point,
where the four valleys converge,

399
00:28:08,958 --> 00:28:10,166
at the same time.

400
00:28:10,250 --> 00:28:14,208
There, we'll form
eight jet transport formation.

401
00:28:14,291 --> 00:28:17,750
On their radars,
instead of eight separate jets,

402
00:28:17,833 --> 00:28:21,208
they'll see a single large
transport aircraft.

403
00:28:21,291 --> 00:28:22,416
Is that clear, boys?

404
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Okay.

405
00:28:29,083 --> 00:28:30,583
Met hotline, sir.

406
00:28:30,666 --> 00:28:33,958
Heavy cloud formation ahead
on Arrow 3's flight path.

407
00:28:34,041 --> 00:28:34,875
Alert them.

408
00:28:35,833 --> 00:28:37,125
Arrow 3, scanners.

409
00:28:37,208 --> 00:28:40,500
Heavy cloud buildup
on radial 030, 80 kilometers.

410
00:28:40,583 --> 00:28:41,708
Exercise strong caution.

411
00:28:41,791 --> 00:28:43,791
Arrow 3, consider alternate route.

412
00:28:43,875 --> 00:28:45,541
Arrow 1, copy. Stand by for update.

413
00:28:45,625 --> 00:28:47,708
There is no alternate route.
We have two options.

414
00:28:47,791 --> 00:28:49,500
Either abort the mission,

415
00:28:49,583 --> 00:28:50,791
or go through the clouds.

416
00:28:50,875 --> 00:28:53,250
In that case, Arrow 3, abort approach.

417
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:55,666
In these mountains,
you are not to fly through the clouds.

418
00:28:55,750 --> 00:28:58,500
Arrow 1, if we abort,
everyone will have to abort.

419
00:28:58,583 --> 00:29:01,666
-That's okay. Arrows, stand by to abort.
-Arrow 3, monitored.

420
00:29:01,750 --> 00:29:03,708
-Arrow 5, monitored.
-…monitored.

421
00:29:03,791 --> 00:29:05,625
Arrow 4, stand by to pull up.

422
00:29:09,541 --> 00:29:10,583
Arrows, wait!

423
00:29:10,666 --> 00:29:12,208
We can make it through the clouds.

424
00:29:12,291 --> 00:29:13,833
Dhali, you've done this before.

425
00:29:13,916 --> 00:29:15,666
Haven't done it in the mountains, Baldy!

426
00:29:15,750 --> 00:29:18,666
If the peak in front of us is over 4,000,
we'll crash into the rocks.

427
00:29:18,750 --> 00:29:20,833
Arrow 4, what's your suggestion?

428
00:29:20,916 --> 00:29:22,500
That peak is 4,320 meters high.

429
00:29:23,083 --> 00:29:25,583
If we maintain 800,
it will take us exactly ten seconds

430
00:29:25,666 --> 00:29:27,666
to reach 4,500 meters.

431
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:29,958
Arrow 4, are you sure
about your calculations?

432
00:29:30,500 --> 00:29:32,416
Sir, they don't call me Professor
for nothing.

433
00:29:34,750 --> 00:29:36,875
Okay, Arrow 4. Go ahead.

434
00:29:36,958 --> 00:29:40,000
But I want all my pilots at Delta Point.

435
00:29:40,083 --> 00:29:41,625
Yes, sir. You will.

436
00:29:43,583 --> 00:29:45,666
Arrow 3, follow my lead. Maintain 800.

437
00:29:45,750 --> 00:29:48,083
Professor sahib, we're in your hands now.

438
00:30:11,875 --> 00:30:13,666
Speed steady at 800.

439
00:30:13,750 --> 00:30:16,083
Altitude 3,250. Climbing!

440
00:30:19,208 --> 00:30:20,416
All right, maintaining thrust.

441
00:30:21,958 --> 00:30:23,916
Dhali, max reheat!

442
00:30:27,291 --> 00:30:28,583
3,750.

443
00:30:29,666 --> 00:30:31,083
4,000.

444
00:30:31,166 --> 00:30:33,250
Visibility is zero, but we're on track.

445
00:30:34,125 --> 00:30:35,125
Five seconds left.

446
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:36,500
4,250.

447
00:30:38,208 --> 00:30:40,583
-Pull up!
-Pulling up!

448
00:30:42,541 --> 00:30:43,791
4,500!

449
00:31:00,333 --> 00:31:03,291
Arrow 3 and 4 at Delta. Joining up.

450
00:31:03,375 --> 00:31:04,416
Well done, boys!

451
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:06,500
Arrows, join up in close formation.

452
00:31:06,583 --> 00:31:08,458
Time to become a dot, boys.

453
00:31:18,875 --> 00:31:21,791
Okay, boys, this mission
isn't there in any manual.

454
00:31:21,875 --> 00:31:26,375
If we pull this off, we'll write
the manual ourselves.

455
00:31:26,958 --> 00:31:28,583
Let's do this, boys.

456
00:31:32,166 --> 00:31:35,000
Transport aircraft flying in
from south westerly heading.

457
00:31:35,083 --> 00:31:37,875
-Details please.
-Currently at 27,000 feet.

458
00:31:38,708 --> 00:31:41,000
What's a transport aircraft
doing here at this hour?

459
00:31:43,250 --> 00:31:45,333
Check the movement sheet.
Tell me which plane it is.

460
00:31:46,166 --> 00:31:48,750
Hamza, check the movement sheet. Hurry.

461
00:31:49,666 --> 00:31:51,625
-You, get the SAMs out.
-Okay, sir.

462
00:31:53,541 --> 00:31:55,750
Arrows, 30 seconds to descent.

463
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:00,125
Nothing on the movement sheet.
No idea what aircraft it is.

464
00:32:03,083 --> 00:32:04,166
Descend now.

465
00:32:09,416 --> 00:32:11,541
Blip is rapidly losing altitude
in your direction.

466
00:32:13,416 --> 00:32:15,125
Dhali, Baldy, it's show time.

467
00:32:15,208 --> 00:32:16,250
-Copy, sir.
-Roger.

468
00:32:16,333 --> 00:32:17,208
Arrows, split.

469
00:32:22,708 --> 00:32:23,916
It's a decoy! It's a decoy!

470
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:26,708
It's not one, but eight jets
coming from different directions!

471
00:32:37,916 --> 00:32:39,958
What are you doing? Why aren't you firing?

472
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,208
Sir, I can't see them.

473
00:32:41,291 --> 00:32:43,375
There's just sound
coming from all directions.

474
00:32:43,458 --> 00:32:45,208
I don't know where to aim.

475
00:32:50,666 --> 00:32:52,291
There are eight jets! Shoot them down!

476
00:32:54,333 --> 00:32:56,125
Arrow 2, missile at twelve o'clock.

477
00:32:56,208 --> 00:32:57,125
Break right.

478
00:32:57,916 --> 00:33:02,083
Missile evaded. Arrow 3 and 4,
clear to fire. Smoke them up, boys.

479
00:33:03,166 --> 00:33:05,416
Those two jets are coming this way.

480
00:33:06,541 --> 00:33:07,750
Give it to me.

481
00:33:11,375 --> 00:33:14,500
In three, two, one, now!

482
00:33:14,583 --> 00:33:16,166
Bombs away!

483
00:33:17,458 --> 00:33:18,791
Bombs away!

484
00:33:53,833 --> 00:33:57,416
Arrows, Ahuja would be proud of us.

485
00:33:57,500 --> 00:33:59,666
Let's get back home now.

486
00:34:05,833 --> 00:34:07,666
For the past two months,

487
00:34:07,750 --> 00:34:11,708
all of us have fought this war together.

488
00:34:11,791 --> 00:34:14,958
The most unconventional war in history.

489
00:34:16,375 --> 00:34:18,333
Today, the Golden Arrows

490
00:34:18,416 --> 00:34:22,791
have completed a suicide mission
with zero casualties,

491
00:34:22,875 --> 00:34:26,166
proving that Indian Air Force fighters,

492
00:34:26,250 --> 00:34:28,291
they just don't touch the impossible,

493
00:34:28,375 --> 00:34:29,750
they break right through it.

494
00:34:29,833 --> 00:34:30,791
Yes!

495
00:34:31,708 --> 00:34:32,541
-Yes!
-Yes!

496
00:34:32,625 --> 00:34:33,500
Victory

497
00:34:34,500 --> 00:34:37,166
is just a few peaks away.

498
00:34:37,250 --> 00:34:39,875
And you, Arrows, have given us the time

499
00:34:39,958 --> 00:34:41,833
to ready our most powerful weapon,

500
00:34:41,916 --> 00:34:43,208
the Mirages.

501
00:34:43,291 --> 00:34:45,458
Their laser-guided bombs are live,

502
00:34:45,541 --> 00:34:49,250
locked, and loaded to conquer Tiger Hill.

503
00:34:49,333 --> 00:34:52,458
Boys, for the past several days,
we've just been hearing stories

504
00:34:52,541 --> 00:34:56,541
of system errors
and the struggles of our fellow soldiers.

505
00:34:56,625 --> 00:34:57,791
But now,

506
00:34:58,500 --> 00:35:00,541
our own laser-guided bombs are ready.

507
00:35:01,250 --> 00:35:04,625
During this conflict, the frustration
and fury that has built up inside us

508
00:35:05,333 --> 00:35:06,916
is no less than any bomb.

509
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:09,916
Battle Axes, are you ready
to deal the final blow

510
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,000
-to the enemy in this war?
-Yes, sir!

511
00:35:12,083 --> 00:35:15,625
-Vanquish the enemy!
-Vanquish the enemy!

512
00:35:36,500 --> 00:35:37,958
Nambiar, laser on. Ready?

513
00:35:38,041 --> 00:35:39,125
I'm more than ready, sir.

514
00:35:39,208 --> 00:35:41,166
Ten kilometers away. Start zooming in.

515
00:35:43,458 --> 00:35:44,750
Visual acquired.

516
00:35:44,833 --> 00:35:46,333
Enemy sangars clear as day.

517
00:35:46,416 --> 00:35:49,083
Let's crush the ego
of little Pakistan once and for all.

518
00:35:49,166 --> 00:35:51,416
Roger. Bombs away.

519
00:35:51,500 --> 00:35:53,083
Bombs away.

520
00:35:57,291 --> 00:35:59,833
After nearly 11 hours
of relentless combat,

521
00:35:59,916 --> 00:36:03,333
supported by precision strikes
from Indian Air Force Mirage jets,

522
00:36:03,416 --> 00:36:06,583
Indian forces have recaptured Tiger Hill.

523
00:36:06,666 --> 00:36:09,125
This decisive victory
restores Indian control

524
00:36:09,208 --> 00:36:11,208
over the strategic heights of Drass,

525
00:36:11,291 --> 00:36:14,500
marking a significant turning point
in the Kargil conflict.

526
00:36:14,583 --> 00:36:17,541
Along with Tiger Hill,
the Indian Air Force's Mirage jets

527
00:36:17,625 --> 00:36:21,541
also attacked the Pakistani supply base
at Muntho Dhalo in the Batalik sector,

528
00:36:21,625 --> 00:36:24,500
in which about
300 Pakistani soldiers were killed.

529
00:36:31,166 --> 00:36:32,625
Where is Mian sahib?

530
00:36:32,708 --> 00:36:37,125
Mian sahib has left
for Washington D.C., all by himself.

531
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:46,416
Thank you for agreeing to see me today.

532
00:36:46,500 --> 00:36:48,708
You barged in here

533
00:36:48,791 --> 00:36:51,583
and blackmailed me
with the threat of nuclear war.

534
00:36:53,333 --> 00:36:56,041
I'm sorry. Nuclear war?
I don't follow, Mr. President.

535
00:36:57,750 --> 00:36:59,166
Either you are a very good actor

536
00:36:59,250 --> 00:37:01,791
or you have no idea
what's happening in your own backyard.

537
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:05,875
Your army has mobilized nuclear assets.

538
00:37:05,958 --> 00:37:07,541
We are tracking them right now.

539
00:37:10,500 --> 00:37:13,833
I don't know what you're talking about.
I promise, Mr. President.

540
00:37:13,916 --> 00:37:15,500
I told you before, Nawaz,

541
00:37:15,583 --> 00:37:19,333
I need to speak with whoever is in charge,
whoever runs your country.

542
00:37:19,416 --> 00:37:21,083
I'm in charge.

543
00:37:22,166 --> 00:37:24,541
I'm here with the mandate
of people of Pakistan.

544
00:37:24,625 --> 00:37:27,500
And it's that mandate
you're looking to protect by coming here?

545
00:37:27,583 --> 00:37:28,625
Yes. Of course.

546
00:37:28,708 --> 00:37:30,083
Let me be very clear.

547
00:37:30,750 --> 00:37:33,916
Unless you came here to announce
the unilateral withdrawal

548
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:37,291
of your troops from Indian territory,
we don't have much to talk about.

549
00:37:39,583 --> 00:37:41,375
I can withdraw my troops.

550
00:37:43,500 --> 00:37:47,000
But I have to show something
to my people, for this conflict.

551
00:37:48,458 --> 00:37:51,166
And only you can help me,
Mr. President, with this.

552
00:37:53,041 --> 00:37:54,125
Let me get this straight.

553
00:37:54,875 --> 00:37:58,000
You want me to broker your retreat?

554
00:37:58,083 --> 00:38:00,916
I thought you didn't want
any outside interference.

555
00:38:07,291 --> 00:38:09,208
Mr. Vajpayee is not taking my calls.

556
00:38:09,833 --> 00:38:12,583
And if I return empty-handed,
Mr. President,

557
00:38:13,375 --> 00:38:15,416
the same people who started this fire

558
00:38:17,333 --> 00:38:20,041
will throw me back
in the same fire and burn me.

559
00:38:21,708 --> 00:38:24,916
Mr. Sharif, the United States

560
00:38:25,666 --> 00:38:28,666
will not be dragged
into a civil-military tug of war

561
00:38:28,750 --> 00:38:32,166
between Islamabad and Rawalpindi.

562
00:38:35,458 --> 00:38:37,250
I have two statements here.

563
00:38:37,833 --> 00:38:42,375
One commends you
for withdrawing troops right away

564
00:38:42,458 --> 00:38:44,416
and committing to regional stability.

565
00:38:46,458 --> 00:38:48,541
And the other condemns you

566
00:38:49,250 --> 00:38:52,208
for illegally occupying Indian soil

567
00:38:52,291 --> 00:38:55,125
and threatening world peace
with nuclear weapons.

568
00:38:57,375 --> 00:38:59,208
Call your cabinet,

569
00:39:00,958 --> 00:39:02,625
take your time…

570
00:39:05,416 --> 00:39:08,041
and decide how you want
to be remembered, Mr. Sharif.

571
00:39:17,416 --> 00:39:20,958
After hours of tense negotiations
in Washington D.C.,

572
00:39:21,041 --> 00:39:23,041
Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif has announced

573
00:39:23,125 --> 00:39:25,541
a unilateral withdrawal
of Pakistani troops

574
00:39:25,625 --> 00:39:26,916
from the heights of Kargil.

575
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:29,750
The Kargil war is now effectively over,

576
00:39:29,833 --> 00:39:31,791
and India has won.

577
00:39:31,875 --> 00:39:34,416
My ISI sources say

578
00:39:35,291 --> 00:39:38,333
Mian sahib is preparing
to pin the whole blame on you.

579
00:39:39,833 --> 00:39:41,458
There's talk of a court-martial.

580
00:39:43,583 --> 00:39:44,875
We lost this war, sir.

581
00:39:48,583 --> 00:39:50,750
General Mahmud, you worry too much.

582
00:39:53,333 --> 00:39:56,041
We've lost Kargil, not Pakistan.

583
00:39:56,625 --> 00:39:59,958
Get the fear of a court-martial
out of your mind…

584
00:40:02,791 --> 00:40:05,125
and start preparing to impose martial law.

585
00:40:07,833 --> 00:40:09,583
There's a huge uproar in Pakistan.

586
00:40:09,666 --> 00:40:12,791
The Pakistan Army claims
that they were winning the war

587
00:40:12,875 --> 00:40:16,708
until Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif
buckled under US pressure.

588
00:40:16,791 --> 00:40:18,541
This news is spreading rapidly,

589
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:22,541
and effigies of the Prime Minister
are being burnt in many cities.

590
00:40:22,625 --> 00:40:26,625
The families of Pakistani soldiers
are demanding answers from the government.

591
00:40:26,708 --> 00:40:29,125
Are their loved ones alive or not?

592
00:40:31,375 --> 00:40:32,208
Sir.

593
00:40:32,833 --> 00:40:35,083
The Pakistan Army
is refusing to accept the bodies.

594
00:40:35,875 --> 00:40:37,791
Bury them according to their religion.

595
00:40:38,416 --> 00:40:40,458
-But, sir--
-They were soldiers.

596
00:40:40,541 --> 00:40:42,125
They might have forgotten this,

597
00:40:43,916 --> 00:40:45,083
but not us.

598
00:40:46,666 --> 00:40:49,208
There's a difference

599
00:40:50,458 --> 00:40:51,458
between us and them.

600
00:40:53,166 --> 00:40:54,958
-Right?
-Yes, sahib!

601
00:40:55,875 --> 00:40:58,083
Climbing treacherous heights

602
00:40:58,166 --> 00:41:00,166
and fighting a brutal war,

603
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:05,083
our army pushed them back,

604
00:41:05,583 --> 00:41:07,208
proving once and for all…

605
00:41:08,958 --> 00:41:11,208
the devastating cost

606
00:41:11,958 --> 00:41:13,666
of crossing swords

607
00:41:14,458 --> 00:41:15,791
with us.

608
00:42:05,166 --> 00:42:06,500
When were you gonna tell me?

609
00:42:07,583 --> 00:42:08,750
Post delivery?

610
00:42:10,791 --> 00:42:13,000
The day you didn't have a sortie.

611
00:42:18,166 --> 00:42:20,500
-Congratulations, Madhavi.
-Thank you, sir.

612
00:42:35,083 --> 00:42:36,458
Could you hear the sound?

613
00:42:37,541 --> 00:42:38,416
Loud and clear.

614
00:42:50,833 --> 00:42:52,000
The Indian Air Force

615
00:42:52,083 --> 00:42:55,625
has played a crucial role
in the victory of Kargil.

616
00:42:55,708 --> 00:42:57,958
So, how are you all feeling?

617
00:42:58,500 --> 00:43:00,250
Look, we're razor blades.

618
00:43:01,375 --> 00:43:04,000
Our job is to cut
whenever and wherever we're told.

619
00:43:04,791 --> 00:43:08,125
Thinking or feeling isn't part of the job.

620
00:43:08,208 --> 00:43:10,125
Sir, what was it like to lose

621
00:43:10,208 --> 00:43:12,166
Squadron Leader Ahuja
in the initial days

622
00:43:12,250 --> 00:43:13,541
of the operation?

623
00:43:14,916 --> 00:43:16,791
Sir, this is my question too.

624
00:43:16,875 --> 00:43:19,250
Ahuja sir could've turned back
if he wanted to.

625
00:43:19,875 --> 00:43:22,791
But was he right to act

626
00:43:22,875 --> 00:43:24,083
beyond the call of duty?

627
00:43:24,791 --> 00:43:28,083
Because of his decision,
we not only lost a jet,

628
00:43:28,166 --> 00:43:30,791
but we also lost a highly valuable pilot.

629
00:43:30,875 --> 00:43:33,208
Sir, I just want to know your opinion.

630
00:43:35,583 --> 00:43:36,916
Sir, may I?

631
00:43:39,041 --> 00:43:40,083
Sure.

632
00:43:41,833 --> 00:43:45,250
Have any of you
ever been inside a MiG-21 cockpit?

633
00:43:45,333 --> 00:43:46,333
No, sir.

634
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:50,375
I'll tell you what a MiG-21

635
00:43:50,458 --> 00:43:53,583
means to a fighter pilot.

636
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:57,625
First, I will strap you into a seat

637
00:43:57,708 --> 00:43:59,041
from which you cannot move.

638
00:43:59,625 --> 00:44:01,958
Then I'll place a few hundred controls

639
00:44:02,041 --> 00:44:05,083
and about 4,000 liters
of fuel all around you.

640
00:44:05,166 --> 00:44:06,583
A tiny spark

641
00:44:07,208 --> 00:44:09,125
can turn your jet into a bomb.

642
00:44:09,208 --> 00:44:13,250
And you're expected to fly this live bomb
faster than the speed of sound.

643
00:44:13,333 --> 00:44:14,416
Small mistake,

644
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:17,333
and you can turn into ash.

645
00:44:17,416 --> 00:44:20,750
This is what a MiG-21 fighter pilot

646
00:44:20,833 --> 00:44:22,000
faces every single day.

647
00:44:22,625 --> 00:44:24,041
Now I want to ask you, sir.

648
00:44:24,875 --> 00:44:28,750
If you were in that cockpit that day,
what would've been your first priority?

649
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:30,250
-To stay alive, sir.
-To stay alive.

650
00:44:30,333 --> 00:44:31,375
Exactly, sir.

651
00:44:31,458 --> 00:44:33,541
That day, in that situation,

652
00:44:33,625 --> 00:44:36,000
Flight Commander
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja

653
00:44:36,083 --> 00:44:39,458
chose to put someone else's survival
ahead of his own life.

654
00:44:44,833 --> 00:44:46,333
No one has the right

655
00:44:47,125 --> 00:44:49,916
to question whether he did right or wrong.

656
00:44:53,750 --> 00:44:54,875
Any more questions?

657
00:44:55,750 --> 00:44:57,000
-No, sir.
-No, sir.

658
00:44:57,083 --> 00:44:58,041
Jai Hind.

659
00:45:39,666 --> 00:45:40,666
Tony?

660
00:45:43,416 --> 00:45:45,125
He went to Delhi.

661
00:45:45,208 --> 00:45:46,125
Paperwork.

662
00:45:56,041 --> 00:45:57,875
Happy landings, boys.

663
00:46:36,291 --> 00:46:37,125
Tony?

664
00:46:43,250 --> 00:46:44,500
How are you?

665
00:46:50,916 --> 00:46:54,333
I spoke to Kamal on the phone yesterday.
She didn't tell me.

666
00:47:00,458 --> 00:47:01,541
Alka, you know…

667
00:47:04,333 --> 00:47:05,166
I'm…

668
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:08,125
very sorry.

669
00:47:10,666 --> 00:47:12,208
The thing is…

670
00:47:14,333 --> 00:47:17,333
I couldn't muster the courage to face you.

671
00:47:24,833 --> 00:47:25,875
That day,

672
00:47:27,125 --> 00:47:28,833
I should've been there with Ajay.

673
00:47:32,666 --> 00:47:33,958
Had I been there, maybe…

674
00:47:39,416 --> 00:47:40,458
Coffee?

675
00:47:57,083 --> 00:47:58,708
On the day of the cremation,

676
00:48:00,250 --> 00:48:01,708
what I said…

677
00:48:02,291 --> 00:48:04,041
Tony, I was just so angry.

678
00:48:05,708 --> 00:48:07,208
But you were right.

679
00:48:10,250 --> 00:48:14,125
I… broke your trust.

680
00:48:18,833 --> 00:48:19,833
Tony…

681
00:48:22,458 --> 00:48:23,833
forgive yourself.

682
00:48:30,416 --> 00:48:31,958
Look, the truth is

683
00:48:32,041 --> 00:48:33,583
that on that day, neither you,

684
00:48:33,666 --> 00:48:36,041
nor I, nor Ankur,

685
00:48:36,125 --> 00:48:38,041
nor anyone else could've stopped Ajay.

686
00:48:38,125 --> 00:48:39,541
That's just the way he was.

687
00:48:40,875 --> 00:48:43,958
Forgive yourself, Tony. Please.

688
00:56:09,916 --> 00:56:14,916
Subtitle translation by: Shrey Ravi

